Sval: LightweightThemeConsumer leaves a window that has unloaded alone

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2083168 (mozilla-central 316632883ed2, Firefox
161), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it.
LightweightThemeConsumer's pref observers could still call _update after its
window unloaded, when the consumer has dropped its document, and _update
threw on the missing document. _update returns once the document is gone.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 161.

diff --git a/toolkit/modules/LightweightThemeConsumer.sys.mjs b/toolkit/modules/LightweightThemeConsumer.sys.mjs
index 2bef680f15..9d3a08e659 100644
--- a/toolkit/modules/LightweightThemeConsumer.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/modules/LightweightThemeConsumer.sys.mjs
@@ -328,6 +328,10 @@ LightweightThemeConsumer.prototype = {
   },
 
   _update(themeData) {
+    // The pref observers can still call this after the window unloaded.
+    if (!this._doc) {
+      return;
+    }
     const manager = lazy.LightweightThemeManager;
 
     // Store user's theme before replacing with aiThemeData or privateThemeData.
